From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:18:49 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Plutonium: the browser panel on Plutonium's browser
 tabs

Folded from:
- the browser panel on Plutonium's browser tabs
- thread tags, groups and the Elsewhere list
- import browser tabs from other shells into a thread
- links and Ctrl+click open in the thread's browser panel
- the server drives the browser panel's tabs through Plutonium's helper
- a page's popup keeps its opener, so OAuth sign-in works
- agents drive windows and tabs
- Preview tools: drag along a path; snapshot images in click coordinates; cursor follows a scaled tab
- Preview tools: the floating preview draws the agent's cursor; resize answers with the new size; snapshots don't flash on screen
- incognito tabs on the desktop
- agent tool fixes: popups in window snapshots, results that say what happened, private tabs marked
- dock sites kept per project or everywhere
- the preview bridge reports a desktop tab's page zoom
- a dock slot holds one window or tab
- native windows are their threads' server tabs
